  "comment": "About 160 species of New York City and Long Island: the 150 bird species with the most research-grade iNaturalist observations created up to 2026-11-09 across the five boroughs (Bronx, Kings, New York, Queens and Richmond Counties), Nassau, Suffolk and Westchester Counties, plus ten heard more than seen (Eastern Screech Owl, Marsh Wren, Clapper Rail, Warbling and White-eyed Vireos, Blue-grey Gnatcatcher, Willow Flycatcher, Yellow-billed Cuckoo, Eastern Whip-poor-will, Saltmarsh Sparrow). Established exotics stay in (Mute Swan, Monk Parakeet): they are what one meets. `packbuilder draft --place 1189 --place 2275 --place 1264 --place 675 --place 1190 --place 142 --place 2410 --place 333 --before 2026-11-09 --top 150 --add ...`. scientific_name and common_name follow the BirdNET+ label file as in us-ca-la (species the committed packs already list reuse their entries); inat_taxon_id is iNaturalist's; wikipedia_url is iNaturalist's link for the taxon. The order is the observation ranking, then the species added by hand. Drafted with `packbuilder draft` and read over by a person; tests/test_definition.py checks the labels.",
